course: dictionary
lesson: 11275
title: Wrinkle: lines, creases and small problems
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A wrinkle is a small line or fold. It can be in skin, in cloth or in paper. «There were no wrinkles in it anywhere.» The word "no" is the clue: the thing was smooth, with no folds at all.
explain: Wrinkle can also be a doing word. «She wrinkled her nose at the bad smell.» Nobody wrinkles their nose because they like a smell, so the words around it show that wrinkling your nose means showing dislike. Try your meaning in the sentence: "She creased her nose at the bad smell" still makes sense.
explain: Wrinkle has an informal meaning too. If someone says, "There's one wrinkle in the plan," they mean a small problem. A wrinkle can also be a clever new idea. Context tells you which: a problem makes the plan harder, an idea makes it better.
fact: A wrinkle is a small line or fold in skin, cloth or paper.
fact: To wrinkle is to make or get these lines, as when a shirt gets creased.
fact: «Wrinkle your nose» means to crease your nose up to show dislike.
fact: Ironing removes wrinkles from clothes.
fact: Informally, a wrinkle is a small problem or a clever new idea.
exercise: «Every gorilla has its own pattern of nose wrinkles, like a fingerprint.» What is a wrinkle? | *A small line or fold in skin | A loud noise in the jungle | A kind of food | A type of tree
exercise: «The deep wrinkles of their skin hold water and mud that cool them.» What do the wrinkles do for the elephant? | Make the skin smooth and shiny | Stop it from hearing | *Hold water and mud that cool it | Turn the skin blue
exercise: Someone «wrinkles their nose at a bad smell». What does wrinkle mean here? | *Crease the nose up to show dislike | Close the eyes to sleep | Sneeze loudly | Smile happily
test:
Dad says, «There's one wrinkle in the plan: the bus is late.» What does wrinkle mean? | A new dance | *A small problem | A large bag | A cool drink
Mum says, «Iron out the wrinkles before the party.» What does she want you to do? | Paint the walls | Count the guests | *Make the clothes smooth | Wash the car
exam:
«The paper wrinkled when it got wet.» What does wrinkled mean? | Very clean | Very loud | Torn into two pieces | *Full of small folds, not smooth
